{
  "version": "2.0",
  "app": "bionodulo",
  "name": "Single Cell RNA-Seq",
  "description": "10x Genomics single cell RNA sequencing analysis with Cell Ranger",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note_single_cell_pipeline",
      "type": "note",
      "position": [
        -240,
        80
      ],
      "params": {
        "text": "Single-cell pipeline: builds a STAR index from a tiny reference, quantifies droplet reads with STARsolo, then clusters and embeds with Scanpy.\n\nCell Ranger is NOT used: 10x distributes it under a click-through licence, so its download URL answers 403 to any unattended fetch and no conda channel may redistribute it. STARsolo is the open equivalent and emits the same Matrix-Market triple Scanpy reads.\n\nData: 10x cellranger-tiny-fastq 3.0.0 (tinygex, 230,610 read pairs, v3 chemistry - R1 is 28 bp = 16 bp CB + 12 bp UMI, R2 is 91 bp cDNA) against cellranger-tiny-ref 1.2.0, both pinned to a commit SHA. The prebuilt star/ directory in that reference is NOT used: it ships Genome and SAindex but no SA, so the index is built here instead."
      },
      "ui": {
        "title": "Notes",
        "color": "#f59e0b"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "genome_fasta_001",
      "type": "input_fasta",
      "position": [
        80,
        80
      ],
      "params": {
        "reference": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/minoda-lab/universc/7cbd039613b45c64f4b6d8219906aafda28dd5f9/test/cellranger_reference/cellranger-tiny-ref/1.2.0/fasta/genome.fa",
        "source": "url"
      },
      "ui": {
        "title": "Tiny Genome FASTA"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "genes_gtf_001",
      "type": "input_gff",
